    docs(node): layer 20 does not establish a started gateway (CF-150)
    
    The layer table's `20 harness` cell claimed the ladder establishes "the chosen
    harness + its gateway/CLI". It does not: the adapter starts `hermes serve` only
    when ~/.hermes/config.yaml already carries dashboard.basic_auth
    (scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh:93-102), and no shipped stage writes that
    file — `node-create.sh --staged-files` prints five files and no config.yaml, and
    no script under scripts/ redirects into it.
    
    On a node created by scripts/node-create.sh the layer therefore ends
    `HERMES: FAIL (n)` and the ladder `NODE: FAIL (n)`; NODE: PASS is unreachable.
    The cell now names only the rows the adapter prints, and a third bullet under
    the table records the unbuilt capability, names CF-150 as its owner, and marks
    the agent-image case `not measured`. docs/OPERATIONS.md §1's create-path
    boundary carries the same statement.
    
    Evidence: docs/audits/code-factory-docs-2026-11-04-layer20.md plus the two
    committed arm transcripts. Gate: bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS.
